      "writtenOn": "2026-02-10T21:55:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Since `VM_DONTCOPY` is missing, this leads to UAF via fork.\n\nWhen you fork with a vma that does not define a `vm_ops-\u003eopen`, the private data is just duplicated without notifying the driver. Since `vm_ops-\u003eclose` cleans up the vma private data, this means that the other half of the fork will retain a broken vma, and any use of it leads to UAF.",
      "revId": "957af3d3cc3d1c6db95936f73dcdaff0a3dd9458",
